/Users/shafqat/projects/silver-bullet/repo/skills/multi-ai-task/SKILL.md:11:Generic multi-model orchestration + consolidation. Dispatch the same task to N LLM models in parallel, capture each response, then merge into a single artifact.
/Users/shafqat/projects/silver-bullet/repo/skills/multi-ai-task/SKILL.md:41:| Latency of slowest model + consolidation is OK | Latency is critical (single turn) |
/Users/shafqat/projects/silver-bullet/repo/skills/multi-ai-task/SKILL.md:46:- **Single model suffices** — adds cost + consolidation time for no benefit
/Users/shafqat/projects/silver-bullet/repo/skills/multi-ai-task/SKILL.md:48:- **Tool execution varies per model** — consolidation assumes same prompt → comparable outputs
/Users/shafqat/projects/silver-bullet/repo/skills/multi-ai-task/SKILL.md:49:- **Output is non-textual** (image generation, audio) — current consolidation is text-based
/Users/shafqat/projects/silver-bullet/repo/skills/multi-ai-task/SKILL.md:87:The skill needs to know how to structure the consolidation. Two modes:
/Users/shafqat/projects/silver-bullet/repo/skills/multi-ai-task/SKILL.md:144:**Conflict-resolution values:** see the full rule library in `rules/consolidation-rules.md` (named rules: `most-severe`, `majority`, `majority-with-uncertain`, `lowest-of-majors`, `longest-with-quote`, `concatenate-all`, `all-collected`, `union-dedup`, `merge-exact`, `prefer-with-evidence-then-newer-then-strict`).
/Users/shafqat/projects/silver-bullet/repo/skills/multi-ai-task/SKILL.md:146:**Schema auto-injection (default ON):** by default, the skill appends a `## Required Output Schema` block to each dispatch prompt containing the schema verbatim, plus a one-line instruction. This ensures models know the column structure even if the user didn't embed it. To opt out (because your prompt already embeds the schema, or you want to manage prompt construction yourself), pass `--no-auto-inject`. The auto-inject state is recorded in `run-manifest.json → schema_auto_injected: true|false`.
/Users/shafqat/projects/silver-bullet/repo/skills/multi-ai-task/SKILL.md:169:├── run-manifest.json          # Inputs, models, timing, mode, schema_auto_injected
/Users/shafqat/projects/silver-bullet/repo/skills/multi-ai-task/SKILL.md:184:3. **Cross-model consolidation** — dedup by primary key, resolve conflicts by configured rule, aggregate scores by configured aggregator
/Users/shafqat/projects/silver-bullet/repo/skills/multi-ai-task/SKILL.md:187:The 4 phases are also tracked in `run-manifest.json → phases_completed` (a top-level array, per the canonical schema in `rules/output-schema.md`) for audit purposes.
/Users/shafqat/projects/silver-bullet/repo/skills/multi-ai-task/SKILL.md:195:The dedup, conflict-resolution, and aggregation algorithms — see `rules/consolidation-rules.md`. These are the core value of the skill; everything else is plumbing. The named rule library (`most-severe`, `majority-with-uncertain`, `lowest-of-majors`, `concatenate-all`, `union-dedup`, etc.) is now formally defined.
/Users/shafqat/projects/silver-bullet/repo/skills/multi-ai-task/rules/consolidation-rules.md:3:The algorithms for the cross-model consolidation phases. Generic — works for any task type that produces a list of items.
/Users/shafqat/projects/silver-bullet/repo/skills/multi-ai-task/rules/consolidation-rules.md:7:## The minimal contract for consolidation
/Users/shafqat/projects/silver-bullet/repo/skills/multi-ai-task/rules/consolidation-rules.md:9:For the consolidation step to work, the model responses need to be decomposable into **items**. An item has:
/Users/shafqat/projects/silver-bullet/repo/skills/multi-ai-task/rules/consolidation-rules.md:82: Build an alias map for your task type. The default (no aliases) is `lowercase + strip-punctuation + collapse-whitespace + exact match`. For semantic dedup (e.g., `AutoGen` ↔ `AG2`), supply an alias map at run time. The alias map is **task-specific** — see `rules/examples/research-prior-art.md` for a 14-entry research alias map. A code-review or fact-check run would have a different alias map (or none).
/Users/shafqat/projects/silver-bullet/repo/skills/multi-ai-task/rules/consolidation-rules.md:87:const aliases = {
/Users/shafqat/projects/silver-bullet/repo/skills/multi-ai-task/rules/consolidation-rules.md:89:  // Add as you discover variants. Persist to run-manifest.json → aliases.
/Users/shafqat/projects/silver-bullet/repo/skills/multi-ai-task/rules/consolidation-rules.md:98:  const canonical = normalize(row.primary_key);  // apply aliases
/Users/shafqat/projects/silver-bullet/repo/skills/multi-ai-task/rules/consolidation-rules.md:115:Mark a row's primary key as `aliases[n] = null` to drop it from the registry (don't count as an item). Generic skip rules for any task type:
/Users/shafqat/projects/silver-bullet/repo/skills/multi-ai-task/rules/consolidation-rules.md:298:## Custom consolidation strategies
/Users/shafqat/projects/silver-bullet/repo/skills/multi-ai-task/rules/consolidation-rules.md:329:**To use aliases in your run:**
/Users/shafqat/projects/silver-bullet/repo/skills/multi-ai-task/rules/consolidation-rules.md:330:1. Build the alias map for your task type (or start with no aliases and add as the models surface variants)
/Users/shafqat/projects/silver-bullet/repo/skills/multi-ai-task/rules/consolidation-rules.md:332:3. Document the alias map in your run's `run-manifest.json → aliases` field so the consolidation is reproducible
/Users/shafqat/projects/silver-bullet/repo/skills/multi-ai-task/rules/consolidation-rules.md:334:**The default behavior** (no aliases) is: normalize = lowercase + strip-punctuation + collapse-whitespace, then exact match. This catches `AutoGen` vs `autogen` and `BMAD Method` vs `BMAD-Method`, but not `AutoGen` vs `AG2` (semantic equivalence). For semantic dedup, you need an alias map.
/Users/shafqat/projects/silver-bullet/repo/skills/multi-ai-task/rules/dispatch-mechanics.md:129:The skill is **fail-soft**: a model failure is logged, the model is excluded from the consolidation, and the run continues with the models that did respond. The skill does **not retry** (retry policy lives in the calling agent's runner, not in the skill core — this avoids retry loops in shell wrappers with 2-min default timeouts).
/Users/shafqat/projects/silver-bullet/repo/skills/multi-ai-task/rules/methodology.md:15:**Schema auto-injection (default ON):** if the user passes `--schema` and does **not** also pass `--no-auto-inject`, the skill appends a `## Required Output Schema` block (the JSON schema verbatim, plus a one-line instruction: "Return your answer as a markdown table with exactly these columns, and nothing that does not match this schema") to every dispatch prompt. This guarantees the model sees the column structure even if the user forgot to embed it. If the user's prompt already embeds the schema, pass `--no-auto-inject` to avoid duplication. The auto-inject state is recorded in `run-manifest.json → schema_auto_injected: true|false`.
/Users/shafqat/projects/silver-bullet/repo/skills/multi-ai-task/rules/methodology.md:19:If a model fails to produce a response (timeout, error, refusal), the failure is logged and the model is excluded from the consolidation. **The skill does NOT retry.** Retry logic lives in the calling agent's runner, not in the skill core — this avoids infinite retry loops in shell wrappers with 2-min default timeouts. Failures are recorded in `run-manifest.json → models_failed` with the stderr reason.
/Users/shafqat/projects/silver-bullet/repo/skills/multi-ai-task/rules/methodology.md:102:Fuzzy dedup is applied at the title level (see `consolidation-rules.md`).
/Users/shafqat/projects/silver-bullet/repo/skills/multi-ai-task/rules/methodology.md:108:## Phase 3 — Cross-model consolidation
/Users/shafqat/projects/silver-bullet/repo/skills/multi-ai-task/rules/methodology.md:170:The user can always re-run with `--schema` to get structured output, or with `--mode quick` to skip consolidation and get raw per-model responses merged.
/Users/shafqat/projects/silver-bullet/repo/skills/multi-ai-task/rules/methodology.md:173:The skill can be re-run with the same `task-prompt` and produce a new consolidated output. It does NOT cache across runs by default (each run is fresh), but the `run-manifest.json` from previous runs can be referenced for incremental consolidation (future enhancement).
/Users/shafqat/projects/silver-bullet/repo/skills/multi-ai-task/rules/output-schema.md:197:One JSON per line per (model, item) — the raw extraction before consolidation:
/Users/shafqat/projects/silver-bullet/repo/skills/multi-ai-task/rules/output-schema.md:218:  "schema_auto_injected": true,
/Users/shafqat/projects/silver-bullet/repo/skills/multi-ai-task/rules/output-schema.md:224:  "aliases": {"AutoGen/AG2": "AutoGen"},
/Users/shafqat/projects/silver-bullet/repo/skills/multi-ai-task/rules/output-schema.md:230:  "consolidation": {
/Users/shafqat/projects/silver-bullet/repo/skills/multi-ai-task/rules/output-schema.md:235:  "phases_completed": [1, 2, 3, 4]
/Users/shafqat/projects/silver-bullet/repo/skills/multi-ai-task/rules/output-schema.md:245:- `schema_auto_injected` — was the schema auto-injected into the dispatch prompt? (v2.1.0+)
/Users/shafqat/projects/silver-bullet/repo/skills/multi-ai-task/rules/output-schema.md:251:- `aliases` — task-specific alias map applied during dedup (v2.1.0+); empty `{}` if no aliases
/Users/shafqat/projects/silver-bullet/repo/skills/multi-ai-task/rules/output-schema.md:253:- `consolidation` — detailed stats: dedup merges, score aggregations, unresolved conflicts
/Users/shafqat/projects/silver-bullet/repo/skills/multi-ai-task/rules/output-schema.md:254:- `phases_completed` — list of phase numbers that produced output (for partial-failure auditing)
